Assembly design profoundly influences product durability, repairability, and material recovery throughout the product lifecycle. How components connect and can be disassembled determines whether products can be repaired, upgraded, refurbished, or effectively recycled at end-of-life. Well-designed assembly allows non-experts to perform maintenance and repairs, extending product life dramatically and reducing need for manufacturer intervention. From a circular perspective, assembly strategy defines whether products can be taken apart cleanly to recover valuable materials or components, directly enabling circular material flows.